orming single or multiple layers. Additional panels show cross-sections of the leaf blade, highlighting internal tissues and the distribution of trichomes, as well as detailed views of individual trichome structure and surrounding epidermal features.)/K 0/P 852 0 R/Pg 118 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj870 0 obj<</BBox 871 0 R/Height 453.543/O/Layout/Width 340.157>>endobj871 0 obj[127.162 305.121 467.32 758.664]endobj872 0 obj<</A 873 0 R/ActualText(Dendrogram showing hierarchical clustering of five olive varieties based on anatomical variables. Two main groups are identified: Group I, including Brétema and Carapucho, and Group II, including Cobrancosa, Hedreira, and Mansa Gallega. The horizontal axi\s represents the clustering distance \(height\), indicating the degree of similarity among varieties.)/Alt(Dendrogram showing hierarchical clustering of five olive varieties based on anatomical variables. Two main groups are identified: Group I, including Brétema and Carapucho, and Group II, including Cobrancosa, Hedreira, and Mansa Gallega. The horizontal axi\s represents the clustering distance \(height\), indicating the degree of similarity among varieties.)/K 0/P 852 0 R/Pg 87 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj873 0 obj<</BBox 874 0 R/Height 137.707/O/Layout/Width 212.598>>endobj874 0 obj[63.2693 620.957 275.868 758.664]endobj875 0 obj<</A 876 0 R/ActualText(Composite figure showing microscopic views of olive leaf anatomy. Panels include transverse sections of the leaf blade and midrib, highlighting the dorsiventral organization with palisade chlorophyll parenchyma on the adaxial side and aerenchyma on the ab\axial side. Additional images show stomata restricted to the abaxial epidermis, multicellular peltate trichomes, trichosclereids, and calcium oxalate crystals. Both light microscopy and scanning electron microscopy images are included, with labeled anatom\ical structures.)/Alt(Composite figure showing microscopic views of olive leaf anatomy. Panels include transverse sections of the leaf blade and midrib, highlighting the dorsiventral organization with palisade chlorophyll parenchyma on the adaxial side and aerenchyma on the ab\axial side. Additional images show stomata restricted to the abaxial epidermis, multicellular peltate trichomes, trichosclereids, and calcium oxalate crystals. Both light microscopy and scanning electron microscopy images are included, with labeled anatom\ical structures.)/K 0/P 852 0 R/Pg 62 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj876 0 obj<</BBox 877 0 R/Height 464.428/O/Layout/Width 340.157>>endobj877 0 obj[127.162 294.236 467.32 758.664]endobj878 0 obj<</A 879 0 R/ActualText(Scanning electron microscope image of a peltate trichome on the leaf surface of Olea europaea. The trichome consists of multiple radially arranged cells forming a central disc surrounded by elongated peripheral arms. Labels indicate the number of cells fo\rming the scale, the diameter of the central disc, and the length of the arms. A dashed line is used to illustrate the measurement of trichome dimensions.)/Alt(Scanning electron microscope image of a peltate trichome on the leaf surface of Olea europaea. The trichome consists of multiple radially arranged cells forming a central disc surrounded by elongated peripheral arms. Labels indicate the number of cells fo\rming the scale, the diameter of the central disc, and the length of the arms. A dashed line is used to illustrate the measurement of trichome dimensions.)/K 0/P 852 0 R/Pg 43 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj879 0 obj<</BBox 880 0 R/Height 223.2/O/Layout/Width 212.598>>endobj880 0 obj[63.2693 149.272 275.868 372.472]endobj881 0 obj<</A 882 0 R/ActualText(Diagram illustrating the sampling and measurement approach in olive leaves. A whole leaf is shown with a transverse section taken from the median region, leading to a magnified view of the leaf blade where adaxial cuticle thickness, palisade chlorophyll p\arenchyma thickness, and total leaf blade thickness are measured. Additional panels show the areas used for stomatal counts on the abaxial epidermis and scanning electron microscope images of the leaf surface used to assess trichome density and morphology\.)/Alt(Diagram illustrating the sampling and measurement approach in olive leaves. A whole leaf is shown with a transverse section taken from the median region, leading to a magnified view of the leaf blade where adaxial cuticle thickness, palisade chlorophyll p\arenchyma thickness, and total leaf blade thickness are measured. Additional panels show the areas used for stomatal counts on the abaxial epidermis and scanning electron microscope images of the leaf surface used to assess trichome density and morphology\.)/K 0/P 852 0 R/Pg 33 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj882 0 obj<</BBox 883 0 R/Height 287.49/O/Layout/Width 340.157>>endobj883 0 obj[127.162 131.301 467.32 418.79]endobj884 0 obj<</Author(Rafael Álvarez)/CreationDate(D:20260419102835+08'00')/Keywords(Olea europaea; leaf histology; trichomes; Galician varieties; bioclimatology; varietal differentiation)/ModDate(D:20260419102835+08'00')/Subject(Álvarez R, Escarda-Castro E, Munárriz M, Álvarez-Esteban R, Álvarez-Santacoloma A and del Río S \(2026\) Microscopic attributes of Olea europaea L. leaves and bioclimatology: the case of Galicia, western Iberian Peninsula. Front. Plant Sci. 17:1783046. do\i: 10.3389/fpls.2026.1783046)/Title(Microscopic attributes of Olea europaea L. leaves and bioclimatology: the case of Galicia, western Iberian Peninsula)>>endobjxref
